  "body": "## What changed\n- `assets/posts/carvera.cps` reads the `Smoothing` / `SmoothingMode` PARAMs (#616). When an operation asks for smoothing it writes one comment per program, `(SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - NO CARVERA FORM STATED)`, at the end of the section preamble (after the coolant word, before the first move). The wording and placement follow `mazak.cps`. The ask resets at section end.\n- No smoothing word is written. The Carvera firmware's supported-codes tables (carvera-community.gitbook.io, firmware -> supported commands -> GCodes / MCodes) list no blending word: no G64, G61, G5.1 or similar.\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/757-carvera-smoothing.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- New pin: `crates/app/tests/smoothing.rs::carvera_names_the_ask_once_and_otherwise_posts_the_off_program`. For both a finish ask and a rough ask, the note appears exactly once and before the first cut, no G64/G61/G5.1/G187 is written, and the program with the note removed is byte-identical to the smoothing-off program. It fails without the post change and passes with it.\n- `smoothing` (7/7), `carvera_post` (4/4), `conformance` (6/6, including `every_builtin_posts_every_golden_byte_exact`) all pass. The Carvera golden `golden/nc/carvera/two_tool_pocket.nc` is unchanged, which proves smoothing off is byte-identical. The existing `off_is_byte_identical_and_writes_no_smoothing_word` now covers Carvera too.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test smoothing -- -D warnings` is clean.\n- No new golden was added: the smoothing suite pins its dialects with assertions, not goldens. The unchanged Carvera golden pins the off case.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Not run on a real Carvera. The change adds a comment line only.\n- Full quick/batch tier not run; only the suites named above.\n\nFork synced at v0.16.0 (branched from upstream/main 5fd45923).\n\nChangelog: Carvera post names a per-operation smoothing ask with a one-time \"SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN\" note instead of silently dropping it (the firmware has no blending word)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #757\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
